      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So some clarification on what I meant by mutual friends since it seems to have confused some.\n\nIf you have a mutual friend with someone it means that you both have a friend in common on your friends list. They don’t need to be in the room. They don’t need to be online. They just need to be on your friends list.\n\nExample:\n\nI make a Friends+ room with the default 2 mutual friends limit. My friend Tom is in the room. His friend Harry wants in. I don’t know Harry, Harry doesn’t know me.\n\nA - Harry and I only have ONE friend in common, that’s Tom. Harry CANNOT join on Tom to get in. \n\nB - Harry and I are BOTH friends with Tom AND Dick. Dick is offline having a wank. Harry CAN still join on Tom to get in.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
