  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-12-14T23:13:42.784Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right now anyone can enter your Friends+ worlds so long as they’re friends with someone inside. This can potentially end with a bunch of random people you don’t know or trust in your world.\n\nBy contrast ‘Friends Only’ is a little too restrictive. People within your social groups can’t get in unless they’re on your friends list.\n\nWith the UI changes coming I thought a sleeker more functional design would be to merge 'Friends Only' and ‘Friends+’ into just ‘Friends+’ but you pick a value for the number of mutual friends you must have in common for someone to get in.\n\nDefault value is 2 – If you share 2 friends with the someone then they can get in\n\nYou can raise the value to make a world more restrictive\n\n1 – Is the same as Friends+ currently functions\n\nMax value - Friends Only\n\n\nEdit: I can't math",
